  "title": "Hashim Thaçi Jails Over War Crimes in Kosovo",
  "summary": "Hashim Thaçi, the former president of Kosovo, was sentenced to 25 years in prison after being found guilty of war crimes, including arbitrary detention, torture, and murder, during his time as a senior commander of the Kosovo Liberation Army.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Hashim Thaçi, 58, was convicted by a tribunal in The Hague for crimes committed while he was senior commander of the Kosovo Liberation Army.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Hashim Thaçi was sentenced to 25 years in prison after a tribunal ruled he was responsible for arbitrary detention, torture, and 96 murders.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The European-backed Kosovo Specialist Chambers, convicted Thaci, and three other former senior commanders of 96 murders were also sentenced.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
